{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/538639-beast-musings","id":538639,"title":"Beast musings.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-03T11:37:49-07:00","id":538639,"title":"Beast musings.","content":"Can a Nightmare form for something that does not exist?<br /> <br /> See, I was thinking. The Beast preview is out, and I've been enjoying it, but it left me with this unpleasant aftertaste in a few ways.<br /> <br /> 1: It felt like the 1st Edition of nWoD Mage. Too many answers. Too many objective statements. Not enough information presented as an IC perspective.<br /> <br /> 2: The Beast crossover mechanics felt somewhat... insulting I guess? It felt like Beast was taking the role of the smarter, more socially adept older sibling. This might be okay in a Beast only game, but speaking for myself at least, it would certainly rub me the wrong way as the player of a different splat.<br /> <br /> 3: It felt like Beast was pulling in two directions. They are creatures of Legend (literally even. Hah). They are the creatures of our darkest Nightmares. But the are also the incomprehensible progenitor. One of these three felt really boring to me. Here's a hint. It's the one that isn't tied to a Beast mechanics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, just for the hell of it, I'm posting my musings on the subject. 'Cause why not?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What came first, Fenris, or Fenris-Ur? Humans knew. On some level, they knew. The Wolf was out there. It was mighty, It was implacable. It could not be stopped, could not be killed, could not even be beaten. So we turned to dreams.We created Fenris. We chained him, buried him, and tried to forget him. Tried. It's the way we deal with things. Lock them up and dream them safe and secure. Then we tell stories. And in the stories, Heroes win. The beasts are defeated, and humanity is saved. And these stories build and develop, and form patterns and take on lives of their own. By now, the fear that motivated them is hardly even noticeable on the subconscious level. It's there all right, but it's real cause is long forgotten.<br /> <br /> And then time passes.We slowly become aware of other things. There are hints, here and there, scattered around the periphery of our existence of the other. Vampires, Werewolves, Mages. The Lost, the Created, even the Dead and Not-Quite-Dead. They're all out there, hidden. Waiting, just like it was in the old days. So our mind searches for answers. has been searching for answers. And there, nestled away in the darkest recesses, it finds the Wolf. The Thing in the Darkness. The Presence Above, The Unstoppable Force. The Dreaming Deeps. The Unspeakable Horror. All built long, long ago to explain why the world was as it was. It finds the Beast. And the Beast is waiting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What did I hope to express with that? I guess it's that Beast clicked the most for me when it was dealing with their involvement with the patterns of myth. When it didn't really explain anything. So, to cut from the purple prose. In this view, Beasts aren't really the progenitor monster. They are what we imagine the progenitor monster as being, so we don't need to deal with what they truly were/are. Are they still &quot;related&quot; to all the other splats? Sure! Humans want answers. They want things to follow patterns and have explanations. It just makes sense that they want there to be a point of descent. So while Beasts aren't actually the aforementioned point of descent. they still have the connections, and the connections are very real.<br /> <br /> In this view, the Beast is not:<br /> <br /> 1: The Missing Link. The Dark Mother may or may not be real, but it didn't make the Beast's, at least not directly. That would be too convenient, and in my experience, in a good WoD game, convenience is only for stories or lies.<br /> <br /> 2: The Elder-Cousin. After all, they aren't from the Dark Mother. And honestly, they have no idea if anyone else is either. That doesn't mean they don't think they are of course. Because that's what they are in the stories, and they are, after all: the monsters in the stories.<br /> <br /> In this view, the Beast is:<br /> <br /> 1: The Human Explanation. It's not like Beasts lose their crossover mechanics, But Beasts don't have said mechanics because they came first, they have them because that;s what they story said they should have. What the Nightmare demanded they be capable of.<br /> <br /> 2: Our Own Creation. We made the Beasts. To explain and label our fears. To be the Monster in the Story. Sure, they weren't really the real monster, but they were everything we feared the real monster was.<br /> <br /> 3: Always and Ultimately Human. After all, we made them. They are a product of the Temenos, of the Primordial Dream. They are how we understand our deepest, oldest fears, as well as how we shape and understand our new terrors. And as such, they are ultimately of us. It is in this central core of humanity that their enmity from the God Machine arises. We can fear falling, but not gravity. We can fear the Gears, but not the Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> <br /> Does this solve all my problems? Not really. But it feels a bit cooler. It answers fewer questions. And it feels like (at least to me) it makes Beast's connections with other splats a celebration of them rather then a somewhat demeaning pat on the back.<br /> <br /> It's also probably incredibly conceited, but this is the internet, and I'm posting my opinion, so that's bound to happen to some level or another. Thoughts? Concerns? Explanations of how I'm wrong? All are appreciated! Particularly that last one actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3172-oraclebones","name":"OracleBones","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T09:38:52-07:00","id":539656,"title":"","content":"After reading some of the Beast Kickstarter text, I was under the impression that all Beasts believe other monsters are there kin because a Beast can merge with the human host through the Merger or the Apex. Thus, at least to a Beast's logic, the supernaturals of today are the children of a Beast Progenitor of the past. Maybe Father Wolf or the Original Vampire were Beasts that reached their Apex? Ultimately it's up to the ST, but Beasts could easily be The Truth, the source of all Supernaturals, the Progenitors of all Monsters. That's what makes them interesting. <br /> <br /> The argument could also be made that Heroes are the Mythic Progenitors of Hunters, but that's a whole other topic. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T13:40:24-07:00","id":539940,"title":"","content":"That is indeed one of the views that could be taken from the material as written so far.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is simply that I personally don't like that part of the material. It directly invalidates large portions of the cosmology put forth by other splats, by basically saying &quot;Nope sorry, we came first and did it better. Your tricks aren't as real as our tricks, and we just know better then you.&quot; This isn't really a constructive view. What I posted was my attempt to resolve this issue, at least for myself, and see what the general reaction to said solution was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3172-oraclebones","name":"OracleBones","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T13:49:16-07:00","id":539944,"title":"","content":"From what i've been Reading i Don't get that... I get they Think that the Dark Mother is the Mother of them all, But.. They Think they could be Related that way.<br /> <br /> Meh Different Strokes too be fair i Like your idea too. Could be interesting (Plus how the NWoD is its possible that it's True. Hell it's Possible that Both are True.... That The Dark Mother inspired the Monsters AND The Beasts are just the idea's Made Flesh from the Collective Thoughts of Humanity LOOKING for a Villian Since the Rest of the Monsters are Hiding.. By This The Heroes are Actually Creating the Beasts not the other way Around... Hmm.)<br /> <br /> Edit: Expanding on the Heroes Creating Beasts/the Inverse Monster theory, Heroes are Horribly broken individuals that are pre/nascent Mages/Psychics/Other that need something too blame, They Retroactively create Begotten as the Focus for all their problems Everytime a Beast has his Homecoming its because of a Hero/Human Calling out in the Dreamscape for SOMETHING too blame. Some of them recover and never have issues again now that the Dispair/Anger Etc is Channeled into something else. Basically... I'm going with the Idea from Beserk... the Manga/Anime, God Exists and is Horrid too everyone Because that's what they Want. In this The Begotten are that. Just another Sign that the WoD is a Horrid place too live and that humans Are the worst of the Monsters, because we make our own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 06-04-2015, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T14:04:33-07:00","id":539958,"title":"","content":"This seems like a good stance to take in a non-Beast game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T14:56:22-07:00","id":540010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OracleBones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/538639-beast-musings?p=539940#post539940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is indeed one of the views that could be taken from the material as written so far.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is simply that I personally don't like that part of the material. It directly invalidates large portions of the cosmology put forth by other splats, by basically saying &quot;Nope sorry, we came first and did it better. Your tricks aren't as real as our tricks, and we just know better then you.&quot; This isn't really a constructive view. What I posted was my attempt to resolve this issue, at least for myself, and see what the general reaction to said solution was.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really seeing that angle. I mean the Beasts think all the monsters eventually come from the Dark Mother, but that isn't really laid out as absolute outside of &quot;Beasts usually think think this.&quot; I mean as far as the other splats are concerned vampires have their abilities as part of a curse from Cain, Dracula, Nosferatu, or something (I don't play vampire, so I'm sketchy there); Werewolves think Luna, or Gaia empowered them; Mages believe their power is just finally noticing what they could actually do and this is a natural part of being human most people never notice; Sin Eaters know their powers come from some spirit thing that brought them back from the dead; and Changelings are pretty sure their abilities either came as a result of the Gentry screwing with them, or continued exposure to the realm.<br /> <br /> Think of it as the Beasts are assuming things work from the angle of literary analysis on monsters. (You know the one that says zombies are representative of the lower class and Andy Warhols &quot;Blood for Dracula&quot; played vampires as representative of the aristocracy that sort of thing.) So the Beasts figure everything monsters eventually dates back to humanity being afraid of something, which eventually gave rise to the different monsters. As opposed to humanity is bloody terrified of people who stopped being dead and like to drink all your blood, or that really angry guy who turned into an 8ft tall furry engine of death, and eventually managed to cope with the fear of those monsters by interpreting them as representations of a type of fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T17:15:19-07:00","id":540179,"title":"","content":"I read nothing in the Kickstarter document that suggested to me that somehow Beasts are more &quot;right&quot; than everyone else and that their cosmology is somehow more correct on the nature of other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 06-05-2015, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T17:49:45-07:00","id":540215,"title":"","content":"Beast cosmology in no way invalidates that of the other splats. Now, the Beasts <i>are</i> related to the other supers in <i>some</i> manner. (Some/Most?) Beasts<i> believe </i>it is due to a common spiritual ancestor. Whether this is true or not is up to you. Could be true, or it could just be a resonance of some sort through the Primordial Dream by way of shared nightmares of the human psyche. OR any number of other things that could be neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T19:32:56-07:00","id":540388,"title":"","content":"Beasts don't have facts. They have beliefs. What they can observe is an ability to suss out certain supernaturals. What they can observe is a special connection with some beings, via the idea of Kinship and powers they can develop from it. What they can observe is that they know there's <i>something </i>in the Primordial Dream which connects to Beasts, and they believe these sympathetic connections between themselves and monsters may have something to do with that <i>something </i>in the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> They believe that this <i>something </i>can be called the Dark Mother, and they believe that this connection with other monsters is a sign that they are all 'related.' however distantly. It's super important to keep in mind the difference between literal and conceptual relation, and that we're dealing with primordial creatures of fear which seem to come from a part of the collective unconsciousness in the nWoD. The supernatural is a lot more complicated than literal lines of descent, and we're getting beliefs here, not facts.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 06-04-2015, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:20:33-07:00","id":540441,"title":"","content":"That is more or less the stance I took when I was considering this post. With that said, my issue derives from the fact that no real alternate explanations are out forth in the Kickstarter preview. Comparing this to Werewolf 2e with it's extreme ambiguity and constant allusions to the mythic nature or the Werewolf origin story, and Blood and Smoke which doesn't even agree on what the Strix are, let alone on where Vampires came from, and it feels a little stifling.<br /> <br /> With that said, I agree, more or less with your points of view. The material was likely intended to be from the Beast PoV, and I really doubt Beast was intended to be the final ultimate explanation on the real origin of everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3172-oraclebones","name":"OracleBones","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T01:04:52-07:00","id":540764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm going with the Idea from Beserk... the Manga/Anime, God Exists and is Horrid too everyone Because that's what they Want. In this The Begotten are that. Just another Sign that the WoD is a Horrid place too live and that humans Are the worst of the Monsters, because we make our own. </div> </div> </div>It's from a deleted chapter of the manga only (Griffith was supposed to talk with The Idea of Evil, which is essentially God in the Berserk universe, before his transformation to Femto), though that's a really cool way to look into things for the nwod. I still subscribe to the idea that Beasts come first and Heroes after, though I am very interested atm at seeing how Demons and Beasts react to each other and <i>why</i> they do it as they do.<br /> <br /> Demons can be cowed down or spooked by a Beast given the latter has enough power to do so over the Demon's Primum... But then a Beast that fails a Conflict of Wills has to hand over some personal info to the Demon and is generally leveraged against them... They're <i>not</i> related, that is <i>very</i> clear in the corebook... So, what's up with that and what is it about the Primum that messes with a Beast's head so much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T11:22:29-07:00","id":547360,"title":"","content":"One thing that bothers me somewhat is that Beasts are said not to have a global organization, but seemingly still all share some beliefs, social conventions, and such.<br /> Besides, why would they not form a greater society? They're one of the only splats with a predisposition for liking and accepting each other, while Vampires have world-spanning Covenants while barely being able to tolerate each other!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T11:41:05-07:00","id":547372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/538639-beast-musings?p=547360#post547360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that bothers me somewhat is that Beasts are said not to have a global organization, but seemingly still all share some beliefs, social conventions, and such.<br /> Besides, why would they not form a greater society? They're one of the only splats with a predisposition for liking and accepting each other, while Vampires have world-spanning Covenants while barely being able to tolerate each other!</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because they are Rarer then Most of the Other Splats (I'd Say more then Prometheans and Mummies, But Less then Changelings) they don't have a Society because they are Monsters... and Monster Like too work in Small Groups. Large groups of Monsters attract attention, also they might not like all of their Family members, everyone's got a Black Sheep they don't talk to/about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value"